  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "#**Brazilian E-commerce project: RFM approach**\n",
        "In this project, I will analyse the **Brazilian E-Commerce Public Dataset** using the **RFM approach**, a common method for customer segmentation based on purchasing behaviour:\n",
        "\n",
        "- **R — Recency:** how recently a customer made a purchase.\n",
        "- **F — Frequency:** how often a customer makes purchases.\n",
        "- **M — Monetary:** how much money a customer has spent.\n",
        "\n",
        "Using these three metrics, I will segment customers into groups such as loyal customers, high-value customers, and customers at risk of becoming inactive. This analysis aims to provide a better understanding of customer purchasing behaviour within the Brazilian e-commerce dataset.\n",
        "\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "2yxAoPxThOGH"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "##**1. Data Preparation & Data Quality**\n",
        "\n",
        "Before performing the RFM analysis, the dataset was explored to understand its structure, identify potential data quality issues, and determine which records should be included.\n",
        "\n",
        "The analysis uses the Brazilian E-Commerce Public Dataset by Olist, which contains information about orders, customers, payments, and other aspects of e-commerce transactions.\n",
        "\n",
        "This preparation stage focuses on examining the available data, checking missing values and duplicates, reviewing order statuses, and identifying the appropriate customer identifier for the analysis."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "wa5kCxa0KPsx"
      }
    },
