    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "##**3. Frequency**\n",
        "\n",
        "Frequency measures the number of purchases made by each customer during the period covered by the dataset. Higher frequency values indicate customers who have made repeated purchases, while lower values indicate occasional or one-time buyers.\n",
        "\n",
        "Frequency scores (F_code) are assigned based on the distribution of purchase counts across customers."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "yC56tmIEefus"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "# Count the number of purchases made by each customer\n",
        "frequency_list = orders_subset.groupby('customer_unique_id', as_index=False).agg(\n",
        "    frequency=('order_id', 'nunique')\n",
        ").sort_values(by='frequency', ascending=False)\n",
        "\n",
        "frequency_list"
      ],
