    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "This chart shows the average number of delivered orders per customer in each segment during the period covered by the dataset. Higher values indicate more frequent purchasing behaviour."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "RZhsM0-yh7cK"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "##**7. Key Findings & Business Implications**\n",
        "\n",
        "##7.1 Low Purchase Frequency\n",
        "\n",
        "One of the most notable findings is that the vast majority of customers made only one purchase during the period covered by the dataset.\n",
        "\n",
        "This purchasing pattern helps explain why the Champions and Loyal Customers segments are relatively small compared to other customer groups.\n",
        "\n",
        "Although making a single purchase does not necessarily mean that a customer is dissatisfied or unlikely to return, the results highlight an opportunity for the business to explore strategies that encourage repeat purchases and strengthen customer retention, particularly among customers who have purchased recently."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "BidCrkq-iXVu"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### 7.1 Opportunities Among Recent Buyers\n",
        "\n",
        "The Recent Buyers with Potential segment includes 29,993 customers, representing approximately 32% of the customer base and 38.8% of the total payment value.\n",
        "\n",
        "Despite their relatively recent purchasing activity, approximately 96.4% of these customers have made only one purchase, with an average purchase frequency of 1.04.\n",
        "\n",
        "These findings suggest that this segment represents an important opportunity for the business. Encouraging these customers to make a second purchase could help develop longer-term customer relationships and increase repeat purchasing activity."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "qcJawUuBjLcV"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### 7.2 High Historical Spending Among Inactive Customers\n",
        "\n",
        "The Lost Customers segment includes 36,308 customers, representing approximately 39% of the customer base and 38.1% of the total payment value from delivered orders.\n",
        "\n",
        "With an average recency of approximately 394 days, these customers have not made a purchase for a relatively long period compared to other segments.\n",
        "\n",
        "Although these customers are classified as lost based on their RFM scores, they account for a substantial share of historical spending. This suggests that the business could investigate opportunities to re-engage some of these customers, particularly those who previously spent higher amounts."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "4kzv3l0IjqSu"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### 7.3 Small Loyal Customer Base\n",
        "\n",
        "The Champions and Loyal Customers segments are notably small, comprising only 14 and 145 customers, respectively, out of a total of 93,357 customers.\n",
        "\n",
        "Despite their small size, these groups show stronger purchasing behaviour than other segments. Champions have the highest average purchase frequency, while both groups demonstrate relatively high average spending per customer.\n",
        "\n",
        "This finding reinforces the observation that repeat purchasing is uncommon in the dataset. It also highlights the importance of maintaining relationships with existing loyal customers while exploring opportunities to encourage repeat purchases among other segments."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "HPtzn1YFmXtS"
      }
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## 8. Limitations\n",
        "\n",
        "This analysis has some limitations that should be considered when interpreting the results.\n",
        "\n",
        "First, the dataset contains historical transactions from a limited period. Customers classified as inactive or lost may have made purchases after the period covered by the data.\n",
        "\n",
        "Second, RFM segmentation is based on predefined scoring thresholds and classification rules. Different criteria could result in different customer segments.\n",
        "\n",
        "Finally, RFM analysis describes past purchasing behaviour but does not explain customers' motivations or predict their future purchases. Therefore, the business opportunities identified in this project should be considered suggestions for further investigation rather than guaranteed outcomes."
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "PmjaMh7lmxgA"
      }
    }
  ]
